  "query_preview": "..The high clouds passing through this morning has\nbeen thin enough and not impacting temperatures with reading\nearly this morning ranging from the upper 20s to the upper 40s.\nFreeze warning for the Sulphur Springs Valley, Upper San Pedro \nRiver Valley, and southern Greenlee County is in effect until 8 \nam and appears to be working out.\n\n\nProgressive weather pattern through mid-week with both systems,\none on Monday and the other on Wednesday, being dry. This will\nlead to a roller-coaster ride in temperatures. Tuesday morning\nwill see another round of freezing low temperatures for the\neastern valleys. Upper ridge builds in Thanksgiving day through\nSaturday, bringing above normal high temperatures Fri/Sat.\nAnother Pacific trof approaches the area next Sunday. This\nsystem may set up a period of deeper/colder/wetter trofs \nimpacting the area during the first 5 days of December.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (Sun Nov 29 to Sat Dec 5)\nTemperature: Near normal to slightly above normal\nPrecipitation: Leaning above normal (45%)",
